// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row elided_return_no_input_lifetime_admitted (tier 3, `admits`). Found 2026-10-15 while migrating str -> &str (str_by_value_admitted): `fn name() -> &str` with no reference input compiled.
// Logos: the E0106 elision check in sema_decl fires only for 2+ input lifetimes; the zero-input case is left out on purpose ("to avoid flagging legitimate 'static-source functions").
// rustc: rustc 1.98.1 rejects with E0106 ("this function's return type contains a borrowed value, but there is no value for it to be borrowed from"; suggests `&'static str`).
// fix hint: fire E0106 at distinct_input_lts_ == 0 without &self; annotate the stdlib/wql zero-input returns `&'static str` (or `<'a>` for raw-pointer sources). Land after the str flip (deem's wql half carries many zero-input str returns).
package elided_return_no_input_lifetime_admitted;

fn name() -> &str { return "x"; }

fn main() -> i32 {
    return (name().len() - 1) as i32;
}
